# Implementation → deploy → verify (MANDATORY)

## Rule

When you **finish changing or implementing** code that affects **Docker surfaces** (API image, nginx-baked `apps/web/dist`, compose):

1. **Do not** tell the user the work is “complete,” “live,” or “deployed” based only on the **git working tree**.
2. **Do** run the reload path and **prove** the **running** API container and **running** nginx bundle contain the change (grep route in container, grep UI string in `/usr/share/nginx/html/assets/*.js`, or equivalent).
3. If you cannot run Docker/npm on the host, **say explicitly** that deploy was not run and list the exact commands the operator must run.

## Backend (API)

After any `app/` change that ships in `truckerp-api`:

```bash
/home/admin/trucking_erp/scripts/dev_reload_api.sh
```

Then verify, e.g. `docker exec truckerp-api grep -n '…' /app/app/routers/…` or hit a health/read endpoint.

## Frontend (static in nginx image)

After any `apps/web/` change that users see in the browser:

```bash
/home/admin/trucking_erp/scripts/reload_nginx_web.sh
```

`docker compose restart truckerp-nginx` **does not** pick up new JS — the image must be rebuilt after `npm run build`.

## Reporting

Until reload + verification against **running** containers is done, phrase status as: **“coded in repo; not verified live on this host”**.

See also: `.cursor/rules/post-code-change-mandatory.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/rebuild-restart-commands.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/dev-playground-host.mdc`.
